{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You are passing through the border of your brothers, the children of Esav.</b> Even though they are the children of Esav, they are your brothers. <b>בגבול</b> — its border: it has the quality of boundary, and all who come within it are joined to it, as it is said (Obadiah 1:7): ״עד הגבול שלחוך״ — up to the border they sent you; from there on, those who betrothed you — they can consume you." "<b>And they will fear you, and you shall guard yourselves greatly.</b> And what is the guarding? Do not provoke them." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> Rabbah — ״וייראו מכם ונשמרתם מאד״ — Rabbi Elazar said: Woe to the ears that hear thus! For if at the time when they fear you He said, ״and you shall guard yourselves greatly,״ when we fear them, how much the more so. Rabbi Yehoshua said in the name of Rabbi Levi: ״וייראו מכם ונשמרתם מאד״ — you want them to fear you? Occupy yourselves with Torah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 4:14–15): ״ונשמרתם מאד לנפשותיכם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The phrase מבקשים אתם שייראו מכם read as a rhetorical question with אתם as postposed subject, following the Midrashic sense; the transition 'Rabbah' apparently introduces Bereshit Rabbah or a parallel Rabbinic source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:50.857204334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}